   "titulo": "Simultaneous actions",
   "texto": [
    "**V-(으)며** puede indicar que dos acciones ocurren a la vez: 웃다 → **웃으며** (mientras sonríe), 먹다 → **먹으며** (mientras come). Se añade **-며** tras vocal y **-으며** tras consonante; con ㄷ irregular, ㄷ cambia a ㄹ: 걷다 → **걸으며**. It is used mainly in a careful or written record.",
    "The students speak as they smile."
   ]
  },
